{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166","id":"pg_3c1b53e58f425e96bc80def4b95f0172","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kuberwastaken-claurst-docs-tools-md-b0637c97ec34-def4b95f0172.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f516bc7c97425b15b7fa8ae529f23956"],"title":"Kuberwastaken/claurst/docs/tools.md @ b0637c97ec34","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:11:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_50da63b7abb648a6a75139af08d40166"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_19cff8fae7b6d0527df906cfda0e7780864b97168b45969442f96a8ee47c5a85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The goal system lets Claurst work autonomously across turns toward one objective, stopping on GoalCompleteTool with audit, /goal pause or clear, a 200-turn runaway guard, or token budget exhaustion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1a7f2e542e996b03192aed1c6cd17612f3987064883ff836c0726000f4a757f3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"BashTool classifies command strings against known dangerous patterns (e.g. rm -rf, dd if=) for higher risk ratings, and a PermissionRequest hook can intercept any tool call."},{"claim_ids":["clm_22a58ac2c9c91c93398de7aa88837dddfeea7e04904c523a22a4465bbb1997e7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Speech modes like /caveman and /rocky compress model responses (roughly 40-85% token reduction depending on variant), and /normal resets to the standard style."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2e0e5f7a6d9f1ec1f5a71336faac4aa7f1e79ae397037b00e205777436a8354e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Session commands include /resume (alias /continue), /fork, /rename, /export, /rewind, and /session for remote sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_346f0c58b04ed365d3ddf5d299fa3b0bf0feaa1604301d07d0570d912b07fbe2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Headless mode via claurst --print processes a prompt non-interactively and prints the final response to stdout, accepting piped stdin input."},{"claim_ids":["clm_39ab31a988be76c657bde2691e5c06c77cc0624e84d92bcab2736333a7cc26a9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Custom slash commands defined in .claude/settings.json under customCommands expand to prompts when invoked and appear alongside built-in commands in the / menu."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3a476daad836560367f2f649d2204bf5d4d2a8b9742e917a76f875c4fd122d25"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Voice mode (/voice) is an experimental toggle that transcribes microphone input via the Deepgram streaming STT API and submits it as a prompt."},{"claim_ids":["clm_43026c2437b3c2afddb116522d77329be5c6bb4c897744173116a0b31c3510ad"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Effort levels low, medium, and high persist to ~/.claude.json across sessions, while max and numeric token budgets are session-scoped."},{"claim_ids":["clm_433bd0e665cc60db910b3619e95c45a0d627826e16696bc1045edd148ad0b506"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The LspTool communicates with a Language Server Protocol server, supporting hover, definition, references, symbols, and diagnostics operations with a documented input schema."},{"claim_ids":["clm_466fd95989689ba4fc73aa7d1a05bee4d72fed42a1eebec32835395863c0ecfb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Auto-compaction summarises conversation history when token usage crosses the effective context window minus a 13,000-token buffer, replacing messages with a compact summary."},{"claim_ids":["clm_48063b10b557ed9a349dc4938d87132c92550c1aedf262723305f7f72d6ef4cf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"CLI flags --thinking <tokens> and --effort <level> set a token budget and effort level for the claurst binary."},{"claim_ids":["clm_495aaa80f9b4a5c120b727dfd0845f2214910ccbb6758ebc1611f1c0fe057259"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Goal completion requires GoalCompleteTool with audit_summary and evidence arguments; calls without real evidence are rejected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4ca7213cf3e9e81a1243d7df02eb09e5cbec8eae8a738aea9eb27fdfecb47cda"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each user gets a deterministic companion generated by hashing the user ID with a seeded Mulberry32 PRNG; only name and personality are persisted to ~/.claude.json after hatching."},{"claim_ids":["clm_522e8a2968c03d5fe10048d6faa62acd9d7a994a5d4ea6c5aff3e2628604e544"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Managed-agent budget split policies include shared, percentage (e.g. manager 20%), and fixed per-agent dollar caps, with a total budget set via /managed-agents budget."},{"claim_ids":["clm_52b889bfc3f63eb8c8c14374bfc43c5450d97059f8ffe57a35c8fb49ae04c307"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Output formats include plain text (default), json (full message array), and stream-json (newline-delimited stream), with json and stream-json requiring --verbose."},{"claim_ids":["clm_53f188adfbb6c4f1ed7bfc7a68558e8d289dbe3de356db37fa4fc1730b5c7e16"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Subagents spawned via the Agent tool can operate in isolated git worktrees; EnterWorktreeTool and ExitWorktreeTool switch the agent's working directory in and out of a worktree."},{"claim_ids":["clm_584fcc86849411a28eca0eeeecaf101b38ef66f6b48e6b69eadb56b89fb07a58"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Budget-control flags --max-budget-usd, --max-turns, and --max-tokens stop the run when limits are reached, exiting with a corresponding error message."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6733b762436b33065a1c7dfbbc6ee6d9239b61afaebe0ab35da1c0f23b31b7ca"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Compaction can be controlled via DISABLE_AUTO_COMPACT=1 (auto off, /compact manual), DISABLE_COMPACT=1 (fully off), and a CLAUDE_AUTOCOMPACT_PCT_OVERRIDE threshold override."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6ba4dc6472d4cd8507416959b4bf9f2eb352aa17c154dd42dfe4e0c38c94988f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"WorktreeCreate and WorktreeRemove hook events allow substituting an external worktree manager, so worktrees can be Docker containers, VMs, or other directory-backed isolation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_78901356456299872fa2ca031445bf75de9253e28c62fd959a2b279f1ba5b8f9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The max effort level is only supported by models exposing it in the API (currently Opus 4.6 generation); unsupported models fall back to high."},{"claim_ids":["clm_87c48014bd4823b495b83645a55c66e07612c5f331173f0fcf59b13aa9d21c0d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Claurst exposes /thinking to toggle extended thinking and /effort to set a level (low, medium, high, or max) for the session."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8802f0340510e72a20292bb1a177c17d2a2ba9f49d254667ee0c986985ba1492"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Permission modes are default (prompt before dangerous/write operations), plan (read-only), autoAccept (accept all tool calls), and bypassPermissions (skips permission checks entirely)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8a3ef34325bdc95460b02cd80ce2a426ff10f79a00b2c89df57eaf7e7047b0f2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Managed agents provide a manager-executor architecture: the manager delegates subtasks to executor agents running in parallel up to a configurable concurrent limit, and does not execute tools itself."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8eabf17a5b9f167c23a9ebb99e924522552d313a62b6d43320781972c55cf8b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL environment variable overrides the persisted effort setting for the current process, with a warning shown on conflict with /effort."},{"claim_ids":["clm_982b730ff4cab40ffd65e757fe06dd5d6e9a5854a376e6565c6d368a8e54d688"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions are stored as JSONL files under ~/.claurst/projects/<base64url(project-root)>/<session-id>.jsonl, with per-session metadata at ~/.claurst/sessions/<id>.json."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9c2c45d4fc8b4259bb0db32e7bfb1c0dfad8e211b5bcbd6ce542514c8863be30"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The --add-dir flag grants read access to additional directories outside the working directory, and multiple --add-dir flags can be combined."},{"claim_ids":["clm_acab80db2f73df80b3fc2f63dfbc42501ff002b7f253fcd6f02f3bb39d73ceec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The /context command shows token usage relative to the context window, with warning/error thresholds 20,000 tokens before the limit and a blocking limit 3,000 tokens before it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ad003195b52f82a586f406c7a4401505e6003e3ee3aedc5859a7bf371ef5ca73"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The /vim command toggles vim-style modal keybindings (normal/insert/visual) for the input buffer; the setting persists unless enabled per-session with --vim."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bf4ed531b2b6431e4cc53c1b1aef15d52506ad16b43f5de46ebaadac331d2180"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Claurst loads instruction files hierarchically: managed /etc/claude-code files, then user ~/.claurst files, then AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md in each directory from root to the working directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d87868e5634e175f003344728111c95418724c39dcf685725d2018c4842c9429"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Bridge mode keeps a WebSocket connection open for remote control via claude.ai, in either an in-process topology or a daemon bridge where the agent can be respawned."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e4b568c9e858438a2541bd7398803682c2d7707b4c522344f2315e349eae7b6d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A public SDK exports getSessionMessages, listSessions, getSessionInfo, renameSession, tagSession, and forkSession for programmatic session access."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e891e07b63eec75746f8f1b12908dcfa9f9d6cd2f2968eebcb4d6b4442b5aa18"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Companion visual bones (species, rarity, stats, eyes, hat, shiny) are never stored and are always recomputed from hash(userId)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_eb312a6b60e4ca20a42c99357269b5e9e7475ddf9c87a8e195ac0ad37b0e6803"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"LSP servers must be configured in settings.json (e.g. rust-analyzer for Rust); if none is configured for a file's language, the tool returns an informative error."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f22c4532fed5c6546d7b1ec98a81b0a4474b9b2b427eb0cc973e1a1b9c90db4c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tools are classified into risk tiers (forbidden, dangerous, execute, write, readonly) that determine default permission behaviour, e.g. readonly tools are allowed automatically."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f2657c52c8e516bdb3048521ef165ac386ac75319ba0bd7b957067e69645991c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The managed-agents API is documented as a preview feature under active development that may change in future releases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f41fc5beca1e81aa26cfea089e538c04d7d8bedfd2e39486636fb1cb1259c0db"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Plan mode restricts the model to read-only operations; write and execute operations require explicit permission, and ExitPlanModeTool returns to the normal permission model."}],"claim_ids":["clm_19cff8fae7b6d0527df906cfda0e7780864b97168b45969442f96a8ee47c5a85","clm_1a7f2e542e996b03192aed1c6cd17612f3987064883ff836c0726000f4a757f3","clm_22a58ac2c9c91c93398de7aa88837dddfeea7e04904c523a22a4465bbb1997e7","clm_2e0e5f7a6d9f1ec1f5a71336faac4aa7f1e79ae397037b00e205777436a8354e","clm_346f0c58b04ed365d3ddf5d299fa3b0bf0feaa1604301d07d0570d912b07fbe2","clm_39ab31a988be76c657bde2691e5c06c77cc0624e84d92bcab2736333a7cc26a9","clm_3a476daad836560367f2f649d2204bf5d4d2a8b9742e917a76f875c4fd122d25","clm_43026c2437b3c2afddb116522d77329be5c6bb4c897744173116a0b31c3510ad","clm_433bd0e665cc60db910b3619e95c45a0d627826e16696bc1045edd148ad0b506","clm_466fd95989689ba4fc73aa7d1a05bee4d72fed42a1eebec32835395863c0ecfb","clm_48063b10b557ed9a349dc4938d87132c92550c1aedf262723305f7f72d6ef4cf","clm_495aaa80f9b4a5c120b727dfd0845f2214910ccbb6758ebc1611f1c0fe057259","clm_4ca7213cf3e9e81a1243d7df02eb09e5cbec8eae8a738aea9eb27fdfecb47cda","clm_522e8a2968c03d5fe10048d6faa62acd9d7a994a5d4ea6c5aff3e2628604e544","clm_52b889bfc3f63eb8c8c14374bfc43c5450d97059f8ffe57a35c8fb49ae04c307","clm_53f188adfbb6c4f1ed7bfc7a68558e8d289dbe3de356db37fa4fc1730b5c7e16","clm_584fcc86849411a28eca0eeeecaf101b38ef66f6b48e6b69eadb56b89fb07a58","clm_6733b762436b33065a1c7dfbbc6ee6d9239b61afaebe0ab35da1c0f23b31b7ca","clm_6ba4dc6472d4cd8507416959b4bf9f2eb352aa17c154dd42dfe4e0c38c94988f","clm_78901356456299872fa2ca031445bf75de9253e28c62fd959a2b279f1ba5b8f9","clm_87c48014bd4823b495b83645a55c66e07612c5f331173f0fcf59b13aa9d21c0d","clm_8802f0340510e72a20292bb1a177c17d2a2ba9f49d254667ee0c986985ba1492","clm_8a3ef34325bdc95460b02cd80ce2a426ff10f79a00b2c89df57eaf7e7047b0f2","clm_8eabf17a5b9f167c23a9ebb99e924522552d313a62b6d43320781972c55cf8b4","clm_982b730ff4cab40ffd65e757fe06dd5d6e9a5854a376e6565c6d368a8e54d688","clm_9c2c45d4fc8b4259bb0db32e7bfb1c0dfad8e211b5bcbd6ce542514c8863be30","clm_acab80db2f73df80b3fc2f63dfbc42501ff002b7